# Own-wording spells of Dark Matter (2024), all 55. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
# Starship spells use ranges in feet (6,000 ft and so on) and Mega damage, as the source does. Mega Hit Points are only for ships and Mega creatures.
TEXT = {
"Antimatter Mine": ["Range 6,000 ft. A mine (AC 15, 10 Mega HP) detonates when a ship or Mega creature comes within 1,000 ft. Dexterity save, 4d12 Necrotic to Mega targets (half on success). +1 mine per slot level above 4.",
 "Range 6,000 ft, until dispelled. You place an explosive anti-ship mine at a point you choose in range. It has AC 15, 10 Mega Hit Points and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. Reducing it to 0 Hit Points sets it off, which can chain into nearby mines.\n\n**Detonation.** The mine explodes in a 1,000-foot Emanation if a ship or Mega creature comes within 1,000 feet of it or ends its turn there. Each Mega target in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 4d12 Necrotic damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You create one more mine for each slot level above 4."],
"Antivirus": ["Touch, 24 hours. A device cannot be disabled by magic, infected by the N-Virus or inhabited by an AI. Hackers have Disadvantage on Intelligence (Data) checks against it.",
 "Touch, 24 hours. You ward a device against digital intruders. For the duration it cannot be disabled by magical effects such as Technical Difficulties or Electromagical Pulse, cannot be infected by the N-Virus, and cannot be inhabited by an AI or similar creature. If a creature already inhabits it, that creature is pushed out into a free space within 5 feet of the device. Creatures also have Disadvantage on Intelligence (Data) checks made to hack the device."],
"Astrogation": ["Self, 10 minutes, concentration. Burn rare spices (100+ CR, consumed) to plot a course. A void jump made before it ends is an assisted jump.",
 "Self, 10 minutes, concentration. Material: rare spices and incense worth 100+ CR, which the spell consumes. By burning them you work out your path through the universe. If you make a void jump before the spell ends, it counts as an assisted jump."],
"Autopilot": ["Touch, 1 hour. A spaceship flies itself toward a known destination by the safest route. It rolls its own saves if no Pilot, adding your spellcasting modifier. 8 hours with a level 3+ slot.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You give a spaceship a limited ability to run without its crew. Name a destination the ship knows, such as the nearest Maw station or a planet. At the start of the Initiative order the ship moves toward it by the safest route. This movement pauses while a creature holds the Pilot Crew Role. If the ship has no Pilot, it makes saving throws for itself and adds your spellcasting ability modifier to them.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 3 or higher slot the duration is 8 hours."],
"Awaken Machine": ["Touch, 8 hours casting. Install a diamond Construct core (1,000+ CR, consumed) in a Construct with Charisma 3 or less or Magical Technology. It gains Charisma 10, Intelligence 10 if lower, and speech.",
 "Touch, instantaneous, casting time 8 hours. Material: a diamond Construct core worth 1,000+ CR, which the spell consumes. You fit an upgraded core into a Construct with a Charisma of 3 or less, or into a piece of Magical Technology. The target gains Charisma 10, Intelligence 10 if it was lower, and the ability to speak one language you know. The GM picks fitting statistics, such as a Single-Task Automaton or a Hardlight Avatar. The awakened machine is Friendly toward you and your allies, or Indifferent if you or your allies have ever damaged it."],
"Circuit Breaker": ["Reaction when a creature you see within 5 ft damages you. 5-ft Emanation, Dexterity save, 3d8 Lightning (half on success). Disables nearby Magical Technology. +1d8 per slot level above 2.",
 "Reaction, taken when a creature you can see within 5 feet of you damages you. Self (5-foot Emanation). You release a burst of electricity. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 3d8 Lightning damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. Magical Technology in the area is disabled until the end of your next turn. Items you wear or carry are not affected.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 2."],
"Commandeer Ship": ["Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. Wisdom save or a Fighter-size ship comes under your control. It repeats the save when damaged. Bigger ships with higher slots.",
 "Range 6,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. One Fighter-size ship you can see in range makes a Wisdom save. On a fail you commandeer it for the duration. Whenever it takes damage it repeats the save and the spell ends on it on a success. While you share a plane with it you override its flight controls. On its turn you can use your Reaction to dictate how it moves and what it attacks. If you do not, it acts as it likes.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** A level 5 or 6 slot lets you target a Personal ship. A level 7 or 8 slot lets you target a Transport. A level 9 slot lets you target a Corvette."],
"Conjure Asteroid": ["Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 hour. Summon an asteroid of radius up to 1,500 ft (AC 15, 100 Mega HP). +1 asteroid per slot level above 1.",
 "Range 6,000 feet, 1 hour, concentration. You summon a spherical asteroid in an empty space of your choice in range. You choose its radius, up to 1,500 feet. It is an object with AC 15 and 100 Mega Hit Points, and it has Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You summon one more asteroid for each slot level above 1."],
"Conjure Shuttle": ["Range 100 ft, 10 minutes casting, 1 hour. A holographic Shuttle appears (Fly 100 ft in atmosphere). Reaches space in 5 minutes of vertical flight. Ends at 0 Mega HP or on recast.",
 "Range 100 feet, 1 hour, casting time 10 minutes. Material: a starship's launch button. A Shuttle (see the Ships chapter) with glowing holographic circuits appears in range. In atmosphere it has a Fly Speed of 100 feet. It reaches space after 5 minutes of flying straight up on most planets, and enters an atmosphere by descending for the same time. The spell ends early if the Shuttle drops to 0 Mega Hit Points or you cast the spell again. When it ends, the Shuttle sinks gently to the ground if a planetoid is close, giving passengers time to leave."],
"Create Vacuum": ["Range 60 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 20-ft-radius Sphere with no air. Gases there are destroyed. A creature without a breathing apparatus that ends its turn inside suffocates and gains 1 Exhaustion.",
 "Range 60 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a bit of kindling. You create a Sphere of 20-foot radius with no air, centered on a point in range. Airborne substances such as poison gas, smoke or fog cannot enter, and any already inside are destroyed. A substance made by a spell of higher level than this one is unaffected.\n\nA creature with no breathing apparatus that ends its turn in the Sphere begins suffocating and gains 1 Exhaustion level. When that creature can breathe again, it removes every Exhaustion level it gained this way."],
"Dark Matter Override": ["Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 hour. A Frigate or smaller ship makes a Wisdom save. On a fail its Speed and Maneuverability are 0 until the end of its next turn, then it saves again or makes a blind void jump.",
 "Range 6,000 feet, 1 hour, concentration. Material: a dial with eleven levels. You try to force a Frigate or smaller ship you can see in range into a blind void jump. The ship makes a Wisdom save. A ship without a Dark Matter engine able to jump passes automatically. On a fail, the ship's Speed and Maneuverability are 0 until the end of its next turn, and then it must save again. If it fails the second save, it at once makes a blind void jump."],
"Digitize": ["Touch. You and up to 8 willing creatures linking hands around an Arcane Terminal or computer move to Cyberspace, or back to the Material Plane. Natives of Cyberspace arrive in hardlight bodies.",
 "Touch, instantaneous. Material: an Arcane Terminal or similar computer. You and up to 8 willing creatures who link hands around the computer are carried to Cyberspace, the plane of neon and data that lies inside connected planetary networks. The spell can also carry you and up to 8 willing creatures who link hands from Cyberspace back to the Material Plane. A creature native to Cyberspace, such as an Artificial Intelligence, that arrives on the Material Plane has a body of hardlight. The GM picks fitting statistics, such as a Hardlight Avatar."],
"Disable Weapon": ["Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. A ship makes a Wisdom save. On a fail one weapon you choose is disabled, and you can switch which one as a Magic action. It repeats the save each turn.",
 "Range 6,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a cork stopper. Pick a ship you can see in range. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail, one of its installed weapons that you choose is disabled for the duration. On later turns you can use a Magic action to change which weapon is disabled. At the end of each of its turns the ship repeats the save and the spell ends on it on a success."],
"Ear Worm": ["Range 60 ft, concentration 1 minute. Wisdom save or the target loses Concentration, is Deafened, and cannot concentrate while it lasts.",
 "Range 60 feet, 1 minute, concentration. You hum a catchy tune to a creature you can see in range. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it loses Concentration on any spell or effect and has the Deafened condition until the spell ends. While Deafened this way, it cannot maintain Concentration on anything."],
"Eldritch Rift": ["Range 9,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 1,500-ft Sphere of tentacled portals is Difficult Terrain. Mega targets make a Dexterity save or take 3d6 Mega Bludgeoning and have Speed 0.",
 "Range 9,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a pickled tentacle. You open many portals to an eldritch dimension in a 1,500-foot Sphere centered on a point in range. Alien tentacles reaching from the portals make the Sphere Difficult Terrain for the duration. Each Mega target in it makes a Dexterity save. On a fail the target takes 3d6 Mega Bludgeoning damage and has Speed 0 until the spell ends or it takes the Dodge or Evasive Maneuvers action. A target also makes the save when it enters the area or ends its turn there, but only once per turn."],
"Electromagical Pulse": ["Self (30-ft Emanation), concentration 1 minute. Magical Technology in the area is disabled. Constructs make a Constitution save or are Incapacitated with Speed 0, repeating each turn.",
 "30-foot Emanation from you, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a bit of frayed wire. With a clap you release a wave of energy. Magical Technology in the area is disabled for the duration. A creature can take the Utilize action to reboot a piece of Magical Technology within reach.\n\nEach Construct in the area makes a Constitution save. On a fail it has the Incapacitated condition and its Speed is 0 for the duration. An Incapacitated Construct repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."],
"Failsafe Spellhack": ["Bonus Action right after a slotted spell fails to affect any creature. You recover the slot you spent. You can cast it and another slotted spell on the same turn.",
 "Self, instantaneous. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken right after you cast a spell with a spell slot that fails to affect any creature. You recover the slot you spent on that spell. This only works if the spell affected no one, for example it dealt no damage, every spell attack missed, or every target passed its save and suffered no effect. The GM decides whether the triggering spell qualifies. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn."],
"Geodesic Shield": ["Range 60 ft, concentration 10 minutes. A 15-ft Emanation of force plates (AC 10, 20 HP) holds breathable air, blocks gas and ranged attacks, and insulates against Extreme Temperatures and Vacuums. +1 AC and +10 HP per slot level above 2.",
 "Range 60 feet, 10 minutes, concentration. Clear triangular plates of force form a 15-foot Emanation that starts on you or on a point you choose in range. The area holds clean, breathable air, and poison gas, smoke and fog cannot enter. It insulates those inside from Extreme Temperatures and Vacuums. Creatures can walk in and out freely, but the barrier blocks ranged attacks, spells and other effects. It has AC 10 and 20 Hit Points. The spell ends early if it is reduced to 0 Hit Points.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Its AC rises by 1 and its Hit Points by 10 for each slot level above 2."],
"Greater Mending": ["Range 120 ft. Fully repair an object up to 10 ft in any dimension, including a broken magic item. Restores 6d8 + spellcasting modifier Mega HP to a ship.",
 "Range 120 feet, instantaneous. Material: two lodestones. You repair breaks, tears and other damage on an object you can see in range, such as a smashed control panel, torn radiation plating, a ruined keycard or a jammed turbine. If the object is no larger than 10 feet in any dimension, you mend it with no trace of the damage and return it to working order. A broken magic item can be repaired if its magic was present when it broke, but lost charges do not return. The spell can also mend a damaged ship, restoring Mega Hit Points equal to 6d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier."],
"Hack System": ["Range 6,000 ft, concentration 10 minutes. A ship makes a Wisdom save. On a fail one system you choose is disabled and cannot be repaired. It repeats the save each turn.",
 "Range 6,000 feet, 10 minutes, concentration. Material: a bit of frayed wire. Pick a ship you can see in range. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail, one of its systems that you choose is disabled and cannot be repaired for the duration. At the end of each of its turns the ship repeats the save and the spell ends on it on a success."],
"Hardlight Battleframe": ["Range 1,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. Summon a hardlight Battleframe and teleport into its Pilot seat. Its Escape Pod lasts 1 hour after the spell ends. Uses the slot level in the stat block.",
 "Range 1,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR and a plastic figurine. You call a Battleframe made of hardlight into an empty space you can see in range and teleport into its Pilot seat. It uses the Hardlight Battleframe stat block. The Battleframe vanishes when it drops to 0 Mega Hit Points or the spell ends, but its Escape Pod stays for 1 hour after the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the slot's level as the spell's level in the stat block."],
"Hardlight Blaster": ["Range 10 ft. A hovering blaster fires at a target within 60 ft of it. Ranged spell attack, 3d6 Force. It can use its own line of sight. +1d6 per slot level above 1.",
 "Range 10 feet, instantaneous. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You conjure a blaster of compressed light that hovers within 10 feet of you and fires a beam at a target you choose within 60 feet of it. Make a ranged spell attack. The blaster is the origin point of the attack, so it can hit a creature outside your line of sight as long as the blaster can see it. On a hit the target takes 3d6 Force damage. The blaster then fades.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 1."],
"Hardlight Chains": ["Range 60 ft, concentration 1 minute. Strength save or Restrained. The target can use an action for a Strength (Athletics) check against your save DC to break free. +1 target per slot level above 1.",
 "Range 60 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You weave light into chains and try to bind a creature you can see in range. The target makes a Strength save or has the Restrained condition for the duration. A Restrained creature can use an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. On a success it breaks free and is no longer Restrained by the chains.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 1."],
"Hardlight Construction": ["Range 30 ft, 10 minutes. Build a Huge or smaller hardlight object (15-ft Cube) with no moving parts. AC 12, HP 30 + spellcasting modifier. +10 HP per slot level above 3.",
 "Range 30 feet, 10 minutes. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You compress light into a solid structure in range. It can be Huge or smaller, fitting in a 15-foot Cube (27 joined 5-foot cubes), such as a bridge over a chasm, a tower above the trees or a patch for a ship's hull. It has no moving parts and cannot directly harm anyone. Whatever you build has AC 12 and Hit Points equal to 30 + your spellcasting ability modifier. If it reaches 0 Hit Points it collapses and the spell ends. On your turn you can dismiss it as a free action.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The object has 10 more Hit Points for each slot level above 3. With a level 6 or higher slot you can use a Magic action to change it into another object that fits the limits. This does not restore its Hit Points."],
"Hardlight Frame": ["Self, concentration 10 minutes. Power armor: Large size, AC 17, 10 Temporary HP at the start of each turn, Advantage on Strength checks and saves, two battlefists (melee spell attack, 2d8 + modifier Force, reach 10 ft), Extra Attack.",
 "Self, 10 minutes, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. Plates of compressed light cover your body as power armor. For the duration:\n\n**Size.** You become Large if you were smaller.\n\n**Hardlight Armor.** Your AC is 17 and your Dexterity modifier does not change it. You can use a Shield with it.\n\n**Temporary Hit Points.** You gain 10 Temporary Hit Points at the start of each of your turns.\n\n**Mighty.** Advantage on Strength checks and saving throws.\n\n**Integrated Battlefists.** You are proficient with the two battlefists. Attack with them using a melee spell attack against a target within 10 feet. A hit deals Force damage equal to 2d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Extra Attack.** You attack twice instead of once when you take the Attack action."],
"Hardlight Gauntlet": ["Touch. Three melee spell attacks on one target: first hit 1d12, second 2d12, third 3d12 Force. A level 5-6 slot adds a fourth attack (4d12), level 7+ adds a fifth (5d12).",
 "Touch, instantaneous. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You conjure a gauntlet of energy and unleash a flurry. Make three melee spell attacks against one target. The first hit deals 1d12 Force damage, the second hit 2d12, and the third hit 3d12.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 5 or 6 slot you make four attacks, and the fourth hit deals 4d12 Force damage. With a level 7 or higher slot you make five attacks, and the fifth hit deals 5d12 Force damage."],
"Hardlight Object": ["Self, 1 hour. Create a hardlight copy of a Bell, Chain, Crowbar, Flask, Grappling Hook, Iron Spikes (10), Rope, Sack, Signal Whistle or Shovel. It sheds Dim Light in 5 ft. Up to three at a time.",
 "Self, 1 hour. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You press light into the shape of one of these objects: Bell, Chain, Crowbar, Flask, Grappling Hook, Iron Spikes (10), Rope, Sack, Signal Whistle or Shovel. The object sheds Dim Light in a 5-foot radius and lasts for the duration. If you cast the spell several times, you can keep up to three hardlight objects at once. You can dismiss one on your turn as a free action."],
"Hardlight Trap": ["Range 120 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 20-ft Cube of hidden traps. On casting and as a Bonus Action later, creatures you choose make a Dexterity save or take 2d6 Force (half on success). +1d6 per slot level above 2.",
 "Range 120 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You lay hidden hardlight traps across a 20-foot Cube in range. When you cast the spell, and as a Bonus Action on each of your later turns, you can set off spikes, swinging pendulums, buzzsaws and the like inside the Cube. Each creature you choose in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 2d6 Force damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 2."],
"Imitation Spellhack": ["Reaction when a creature within 60 ft casts a spell with V, S or M components of a level you can cast. You memorize it for 1 hour. It ends after you cast it.",
 "Range 60 feet, 1 hour. Casting time: Reaction, taken when you see a creature within 60 feet of you cast a spell that has Verbal, Somatic or Material components and is of a level you can cast. You memorize that spell for a while. For the duration you have it prepared. This spellhack ends after you cast the prepared spell."],
"Improvised Spellhack": ["Bonus Action when you cast a spell with a slot of level 5 or lower. Swap it for any spell on your list of the same level with an action casting time, even if unprepared.",
 "Self, instantaneous. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken when you cast a spell with a spell slot of level 5 or lower. You replace that spell with any spell on your spell list that is of the same level and has a casting time of an action. You do not need to have it prepared. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn."],
"Ionize": ["Range 150 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 20-ft-radius Sphere of plasma, Heavily Obscured. Dexterity save, 10d6 Fire (half on success), rising by 2d6 each of your turns up to 20d6. Entering or ending a turn there forces the save.",
 "Range 150 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a matchbox. You heat the air in a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point in range until it turns to plasma. The area is Heavily Obscured. When the Sphere appears, each creature in it makes a Dexterity save and takes 10d6 Fire damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. A creature also makes the save when it enters the Sphere for the first time on its turn or ends its turn there, but only once per turn. The damage rises by 2d6 at the start of each of your turns, to a maximum of 20d6."],
"Local Jump": ["Self. Teleport your ship up to 3,000 ft in any direction and turn it to face any way.",
 "Self, instantaneous. You teleport your ship up to 3,000 feet in any direction and turn it to face whichever way you choose."],
"Meteoroid Shower": ["Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 2,000-ft Cube of micro-meteors is Difficult Terrain. Mega targets make a Dexterity save or take 2d4 Mega Bludgeoning (half on success).",
 "Range 6,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. You call down a rain of tiny meteors in a 2,000-foot Cube, which is Difficult Terrain for the duration. Each Mega target in the Cube makes a Dexterity save and takes 2d4 Mega Bludgeoning damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. A target also makes the save when it enters the Cube or ends its turn there, but only once per turn."],
"Mutate": ["Range 10 ft, concentration 1 hour. A Large or smaller Beast or familiar makes a Constitution save or becomes a Mutant (Avian, Cephalopod or Insectoid) and gains Temporary HP equal to the form's HP. It is your ally.",
 "Range 10 feet, 1 hour, concentration. Material: a sample of radium. You scramble the genes of a Large or smaller Beast or familiar in range. It makes a Constitution save or twists into a hulking abomination. Its statistics are replaced by the Mutant stat block, though it keeps its Hit Points. When you cast the spell, choose Avian, Cephalopod or Insectoid. The target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the Hit Points of the Mutant form, and the spell ends on it early when those are gone.\n\nThe creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count and acts right after you. It obeys your spoken commands (no action from you). If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and moves to avoid danger.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the slot's level as the spell's level in the stat block."],
"Orbital Hardlight Cannon": ["Range 500 ft, concentration 1 minute. A beam in a 15-ft-radius, 1-mile-high Cylinder. Dexterity save, 12d8 Radiant (half on success). Move it 60 ft with a Magic action. Ignites loose flammables.",
 "Range 500 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You shape light into a huge construct, an orbital cannon 1 mile above your head. It fires a blinding beam into a Cylinder of 15-foot radius and 1-mile height centered on a point in range. When the Cylinder appears, each creature in it makes a Dexterity save and takes 12d8 Radiant damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. The beam ignites flammable nonmagical objects in the area that nobody wears or carries.\n\nOn later turns you can use a Magic action to move the Cylinder up to 60 feet. A creature also makes the save when the Cylinder moves into its space and when it enters the area or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn."],
"Overcharge Weapon": ["Self, concentration 1 minute. One installed ship weapon deals an extra 1d6 Force damage on a hit.",
 "Self, 1 minute, concentration. Choose one weapon installed on your ship. Until the spell ends, attacks with that weapon deal an extra 1d6 Force damage on a hit."],
"Phase Shift": ["Self, concentration 1 minute. Your ship goes partly ethereal. Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage to it is reduced by your spellcasting modifier. It moves through creatures and objects as Difficult Terrain and takes 5 (1d10) Mega Force if it ends a turn inside one.",
 "Self, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a flawless crystal. Your ship shifts between planes and becomes partly ethereal. Whenever an attack hits it, the Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage it takes is reduced by your spellcasting ability modifier. The ship can also move through creatures and objects as if they were Difficult Terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) Mega Force damage if it ends its turn inside a creature or object."],
"Ray Spellhack": ["Bonus Action when you cast an instantaneous spell that needs a save. Turn it into a ray at one target within 120 ft. Ranged spell attack. On a hit it auto-fails the save. Legendary Resistance can turn the hit into a miss.",
 "Self, instantaneous. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken when you cast an instantaneous spell that requires a saving throw. Instead of its normal area, you channel the spell into a ray at one target. Make a ranged spell attack against a target within 120 feet of you. On a hit, the target is affected by the spell and automatically fails its save against it. A creature with Legendary Resistance can use it to make this attack miss instead. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn."],
"Recharge Shields": ["Self. Your ship regains all of its Shield Points.",
 "Self, instantaneous. Material: a bubble wand. Your ship regains all of its Shield Points."],
"Sequenced Spellhack": ["Self, 10 minutes casting, 8 hours. Cast three level 1-2 action spells now without effect, then release all three with one Magic action later. A level 6+ slot allows two level 3 spells, or levels 3, 2 and 1.",
 "Self, 8 hours, casting time 10 minutes. Material: a spell sequencer worth 5,000+ CR. Choose three different level 1 or 2 spells you can cast that have a casting time of an action. You cast all three now, each with the lowest slot possible and in any order. They do not take effect yet. These are the sequenced spells. Before the spellhack ends you can take a Magic action to cast them in the order you first cast them. All three count as part of that one Magic action and use components as normal. You cannot cast another spell with a spell slot on the same turn. You choose targets for the sequenced spells as each is cast. The spellhack then ends. Casting it again ends the effect of an earlier Sequenced Spellhack on you.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 6 or higher slot you can sequence two level 3 spells, or one each of level 3, level 2 and level 1."],
"Shield Burst": ["Range 3,000-ft Emanation, concentration 1 minute. Fails if your ship has no Shield Points. When your ship loses all Shield Points, it erupts. Mega targets make a Dexterity save or take 5d8 Lightning (half on success).",
 "3,000-foot Emanation from your ship, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a handful of glass shards. You charge your ship's shields with crackling energy. The spell fails if the ship has no Shield Points when you cast it. When the ship loses all of its Shield Points, energy erupts in a 3,000-foot Emanation and the spell ends. Each Mega target in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 5d8 Lightning damage on a fail, or half as much on a success."],
"Shield Disruption": ["Self (1,500-ft Emanation), concentration 1 minute. Ships in the area lose their Shield Points and cannot regain them while inside.",
 "1,500-foot Emanation from your ship, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a needle. Your ship sends out a frequency that breaks shields. A ship in the area loses its Shield Points and cannot regain them until it leaves the area."],
"Simulation": ["Self, 10 minutes casting. Material: an Arcane Terminal or similar computer. The GM summarizes the likely events of the next 24 hours, ignoring things you do not know or unlikely events.",
 "Self, instantaneous, casting time 10 minutes. Material: an Arcane Terminal or similar computer. You run a detailed digital simulation of the next day's events and gain insight into a likely future. The GM gives you a summary of what probably happens in the next 24 hours. You set the parameters from what you know, so the summary leaves out unknown facts (an ambush waiting for you, a traitor among you) and unlikely events (gaining or losing a companion)."],
"Speedcycle": ["Touch, concentration 1 hour. A force motorcycle (AC 15, 40 HP, seats two) appears. Mount or dismount once per turn for half your Speed. Bonus Actions: Bail (6d6 Fire blast), Driveby (40 ft, Advantage and +1d8 on a melee attack), Floor It (100 ft).",
 "Touch, 1 hour, concentration. Material: a set of keys. A Medium motorcycle of magical force appears under a creature you touch. You choose its look, but it always has two wheels and seats two Medium or Small creatures. You or a creature you choose can operate it, using at least one hand at all times, and one creature can ride along. A creature can mount or dismount once per turn, spending movement equal to half its Speed (round down). The motorcycle is an object with AC 15 and 40 Hit Points. At 0 Hit Points it coasts to a stop and fades, giving rider and passenger time to dismount, and the spell ends.\n\nWhile you operate it you can use a Bonus Action for one of these:\n\n**Bail.** You and the passenger leap off and are Prone. The motorcycle speeds up to 60 feet in a direction you choose and explodes in a 10-foot-radius Sphere on the first Medium or larger obstacle it hits. Each creature there makes a Dexterity save and takes 6d6 Fire damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. The spell then ends.\n\n**Driveby.** The motorcycle moves up to 40 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks. You can split this movement across your turn. If you make a melee attack during it, you have Advantage on the roll and deal an extra 1d8 damage of the attack's type on a hit.\n\n**Floor It.** The motorcycle moves up to 100 feet. If it provokes an Opportunity Attack while you ride it, the attacker can target you or the motorcycle. With this Bonus Action it can travel 30 miles in an hour, or up to 80 miles on an open paved road."],
"Splice": ["Range 60 ft, 1 hour. Take genetic material from a creature (alive or dead within 10 days) and give a recipient within 5 ft one of its traits plus its Speeds, Resistances or special senses. The GM picks the trait.",
 "Range 60 feet, 1 hour. Material: a glass syringe worth 1,000+ CR. A thin beam of arcane energy takes a genetic sample from a creature you can see in range and gives it to a recipient within 5 feet of you. The donor does not need to be alive if you target a part of a creature that died within the last 10 days. The recipient gains one of the donor's traits, such as a ghast's Stench or a dwarf's Stonecunning, and also one of these: the donor's Speeds, Resistances or special senses. The GM chooses which trait, if any, is gained. Only traits and statistics native to the donor can pass over, not spells or gear affecting it. The recipient looks like a mix of the donor and itself. The changes and the gained statistics last for the duration."],
"Summon Hardlight Spirit": ["Range 90 ft, concentration 1 hour. A hardlight Construct appears in a free space you can see and uses the Hardlight Spirit stat block. It vanishes at 0 HP or when the spell ends.",
 "Range 90 feet, 1 hour, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You call forth a hardlight Construct of gleaming gears, pistons, plates and motors. It appears in an empty space you can see in range and uses the Hardlight Spirit stat block. It vanishes when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends."],
"Technical Difficulties": ["Bonus Action, range 60 ft, concentration 1 minute. Pick a piece of Magical Technology in range. It malfunctions and is disabled for the duration.",
 "Range 60 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Casting time: Bonus Action. Material: a bit of frayed wire. Lights flicker, blasters jam and Arcane Terminals crash. Choose a piece of Magical Technology in range. It malfunctions unpredictably and is disabled for the duration."],
"Technomancy": ["Cantrip, range 60 ft. Perform a basic operation on a device you see, such as pressing a button, typing about a dozen keystrokes, or an authorized action. You cannot rewire it or bypass authorization without a Hacking attempt.",
 "Range 60 feet, instantaneous. With a complex gesture you manipulate a technological device you can see in range. You can do any basic operation on it, including pressing an external button, entering about a dozen keystrokes, doing an authorized operation (such as opening an unlocked door), dimming or brightening a screen, or muting a noisy device. You cannot disconnect or reconnect wires, and you cannot do an unauthorized operation without making a Hacking attempt."],
"Transfer Consciousness": ["Touch, 1 hour casting. Needs a gold-plated cable (1,000+ CR) and a vect Construct body (2,000+ CR) or a computer. Move a willing or Unconscious creature's soul into a Construct body, or back up a digital imprint of it.",
 "Touch, instantaneous, casting time 1 hour. Material: a gold-plated cable worth 1,000+ CR, plus either a Construct body made of vect components worth 2,000+ CR or an Arcane Terminal or similar computer. You move the soul of a willing creature, or one that has the Unconscious condition, into a machine. When you cast it, choose one option.\n\n**Transfer Soul.** The soul moves from its body into a waiting Construct body. The target controls the new body if its soul is free to do so, and keeps its memories of its past life and its capabilities. It swaps its species for vect and changes its traits to match. Its old body falls into an indefinite catatonic state.\n\n**Backup Soul.** A digital imprint of the target's soul, with its personality and experiences, is uploaded to an Arcane Terminal or similar computer such as a ship's computer. If the target dies, its soul moves to the terminal, provided the soul is free and willing to return. If a waiting Construct body is linked to the terminal, the soul moves into it automatically as in Transfer Soul, and the backup is erased. The creature recalls only what it knew up to the moment you cast this spell."],
"Transferred Spellhack": ["Bonus Action when you cast an action spell with a level 1-3 slot. Give it to a willing creature within 30 ft instead. It casts it as a Reaction, free of slot and Material components, using your DC and attack bonus, and keeps it prepared for 8 hours.",
 "Range 30 feet, 8 hours. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken when you cast a spell with a spell slot of level 1 to 3 that has a casting time of an action. Instead of the spell taking effect, you hand it to a willing creature in range. That creature can at once take a Reaction to cast it, with no spell slot and no Material components, using your spell save DC and spell attack modifier. If the spell needs Concentration, the target maintains it. The target also has the spell prepared for the duration and can cast it with its own spell slots of the right level, using its own spellcasting ability. It loses the prepared spell if you cast this spellhack again. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn."],
"Turbulence": ["Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. A ship makes a Wisdom save. On a fail its Speed is halved and its Maneuverability drops to 45 degrees if higher.",
 "Range 6,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a fan. Pick a ship you can see in range. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail, its Speed is halved and its Maneuverability is lowered to 45 degrees if it was higher, for the duration."],
"Upgraded Spellhack": ["Bonus Action when you cast a spell with a slot. Raise the spell's effective level by 1, to a maximum of 9. You can cast it and another slotted spell on the same turn.",
 "Self, instantaneous. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken when you cast a spell with a spell slot. The triggering spell's effective level rises by 1, up to a maximum of level 9. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn."],
"White Dwarf": ["Range 1 mile, concentration 1 minute. An artificial star (10-ft-radius Sphere) with 60-ft heat and 15-ft extreme heat Emanations. Constitution save: 4d8 Radiant (8d8 in extreme heat), pulled 10 ft toward it, half damage on success. Touching it deals 8d8.",
 "Range 1 mile, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a pair of spectacles made from darkened glass. You create an artificial star, a brilliant 10-foot-radius Sphere in an empty space you can see in range. It makes a 60-foot Emanation of heat and a 15-foot Emanation of extreme heat. Whenever a creature enters either Emanation or ends its turn there, it makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 4d8 Radiant damage (8d8 if it is in the extreme heat Emanation) and is pulled 10 feet straight toward the star. On a success it takes half damage and is not pulled. A creature or object that touches the star's Sphere takes 8d8 Radiant damage.\n\nThe Sphere gives Bright Light in a 1-mile radius and Dim Light for 1 more mile. If any of its area overlaps an area of Darkness made by a spell of level 8 or lower, that spell is dispelled."],
"Worldseek": ["Self, concentration 1 hour. You know the direction and distance to the nearest planet, planetoid or moon. Fails if you are already on one.",
 "Self, 1 hour, concentration. Material: a spyglass. The spell shows the way to the nearest planet. For the duration you know the direction and distance to the nearest planet, planetoid or moon. If you cast it while standing on a planet, planetoid or moon, the spell fails."],
"Zone of Atmosphere": ["Range 60 ft, 1 hour. A 30-ft-radius Sphere of clean breathable air, or a 30-ft Emanation around an unattended object. Gas and smoke cannot enter. Insulates against Extreme Temperatures and Vacuums.",
 "Range 60 feet, 1 hour. Material: a glass fish bowl. You make a 30-foot-radius Sphere of clean, breathable air centered on a point you can see in range. You can instead cast it on an object that nobody wears or carries, so the air fills a 30-foot Emanation from that object. Poison gas, smoke and fog cannot enter the area, and any already inside are destroyed. A substance made by a spell of higher level than this one is unaffected. The area insulates those inside from Extreme Temperatures and Vacuums."],
}
